___TESTS___

scenarios:
- name: Loads the pinned script and fires success when consent is off
  code: |-
    let url;
    mock('injectScript', (u, ok, fail, token) => { url = u; ok(); });
    runCode({ consentMode: 'off' });
    assertThat(url).isEqualTo('https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/newnorthdigital/bot-signal-web-tag@1.0.0/bot-signal.js');
    assertApi('gtmOnSuccess').wasCalled();
- name: Script load failure calls gtmOnFailure
  code: |-
    mock('injectScript', (u, ok, fail, token) => { fail(); });
    runCode({ consentMode: 'off' });
    assertApi('gtmOnFailure').wasCalled();
    assertApi('gtmOnSuccess').wasNotCalled();
- name: Auto mode with consent granted loads immediately
  code: |-
    mock('isConsentGranted', (t) => true);
    mock('injectScript', (u, ok, fail, token) => { ok(); });
    runCode({ consentMode: 'auto' });
    assertApi('injectScript').wasCalled();
    assertApi('gtmOnSuccess').wasCalled();
- name: Auto mode with consent denied waits and does not load
  code: |-
    mock('isConsentGranted', (t) => false);
    mock('addConsentListener', (t, cb) => {});
    runCode({ consentMode: 'auto' });
    assertApi('addConsentListener').wasCalled();
    assertApi('injectScript').wasNotCalled();
    assertApi('gtmOnSuccess').wasNotCalled();
- name: Loads once when consent is granted later via the listener
  code: |-
    let listener;
    let loads = 0;
    mock('isConsentGranted', (t) => false);
    mock('addConsentListener', (t, cb) => { listener = cb; });
    mock('injectScript', (u, ok, fail, token) => { loads = loads + 1; ok(); });
    runCode({ consentMode: 'auto' });
    listener('analytics_storage', true);
    listener('analytics_storage', true);
    assertThat(loads).isEqualTo(1);
    assertApi('gtmOnSuccess').wasCalled();
- name: Load immediately mode skips the consent check
  code: |-
    mock('isConsentGranted', (t) => false);
    mock('injectScript', (u, ok, fail, token) => { ok(); });
    runCode({ consentMode: 'off' });
    assertApi('injectScript').wasCalled();


___NOTES___

Bot Signal by New North: the browser half of Bot Score by New North (sGTM).

WHAT IT DOES
  Loads bot-signal.js (about 2 KB, pinned release from this repo via jsDelivr). The
  script watches for real input (wheel, touch, key, pointer, mouse move) and for
  scrolling. It writes the session cookie _nnd_hs = "1.<flags>":
    i  real input seen in this session
    s  page scrolled more than one viewport with no input at all (scripted scroll)
    w  navigator.webdriver is true (browser under automation)
  Events dispatched by page code (isTrusted false) are ignored. No verdict on
  reloads, back/forward, late loads after the visitor scrolled, or while an
  on-screen iframe covering a quarter of the viewport can swallow input.

HOW BOT SCORE GETS IT
  Same-site server container (e.g. sst.example.com): the cookie rides along on
  GA4 hits automatically. Other setups: add a 1st-party cookie variable for
  _nnd_hs and send it as the event parameter nnd_hs on your GA4 event tags.

LIMITS
  Behaviour arrives after the first page_view, so use the score to hold back
  conversions and to label traffic, not to block the landing hit. A bot that
  drives a real mouse or wheel is not caught by this signal.

